# GreeterNameInput: typed-username field keys, in Glass, Plain and Material greeters.
# NOTE: $TESSERA_BIN must point at the Rust binary; each style is started in turn and left with Esc (twice if a field is open).
# ===== Glass
setup TESSERA_GREETER_MOCK=1 $TESSERA_BIN --greeter --style look --look glass --demo users &
wait 2
shot glass-start
note Glass greeter with a person selected; "Switch user" (person-with-arrows) button visible beside the name.
ptr move 1100 700 sleep 200 click down up
# NOTE: click on layer surfaces may not register in the harness; the Switch user button position is a guess, compare with the QML position from the shot above (reviewer: if nothing happened, mark MANUAL).
wait 0.5
shot glass-edit
note Username field shows the current name with ALL text selected, same as QML.
key ada
wait 0.3
shot glass-ada
note Typed "ada" replaced the selection (field shows only "ada").
key -k Tab
wait 0.5
shot glass-tab
note Focus moved to the password field and Ada is the chosen person (name above shows Ada).
# Step 2: unlisted user
# MANUAL: click Switch user again, type nobody + Return: picture shows the initial "N" placeholder and the password field has focus
# Step 3: Up returns to the list
# MANUAL: in the username field press Up: back to the list (previous person)
key -k Escape
wait 1
# ===== Plain
setup TESSERA_GREETER_MOCK=1 $TESSERA_BIN --greeter --style plain --demo users &
wait 2
shot plain-start
note Plain greeter, same states as Glass; compare with QML plain.
# MANUAL: repeat the Switch user / ada / Tab check in Plain (click targets differ)
key -k Escape
wait 1
# ===== Material
setup TESSERA_GREETER_MOCK=1 $TESSERA_BIN --greeter --style look --look material --demo users &
wait 2
key x
wait 0.5
shot material-open
note Material pill opened by the key press (one dot); compare with QML.
# MANUAL: Switch user in Material: field 360x56 with the name selected; same Tab/Up/Esc behaviour
key -k Escape
wait 1
# ===== No people listed
setup TESSERA_GREETER_MOCK=1 $TESSERA_BIN --greeter --style look --look glass --demo none &
wait 2
shot none
note --demo none: the username field is shown at once with the placeholder "Username" (no person list).
key -k Escape
wait 1
shot none-esc
note Esc in this state does NOT go back to a list; greeter either stays (field still there) as in QML. Check against QML.
key -k Escape
wait 1
